# Line endings
#
# Forces LF in the WORKING TREE on every platform, not just in the index.
# Without this, a repo authored on Windows and consumed by Linux/macOS
# hands out `.sh` files that die on their own shebang line with
# `$'\r': command not found`, and git's own defaults won't catch it —
# the index can be perfectly clean LF while the checkout is not.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the file types that actually execute.
*.sh text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.bash text eol=lf

# Windows-native scripts are the exception: cmd.exe and PowerShell want CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf
*.ps1 text eol=crlf

# Archives and images — say so explicitly so `text=auto` above can never
# guess wrong and rewrite bytes inside one.
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.pdf binary
*.skill binary
